From e1dd7019bd511d30df50a969b54b71967826f00c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 06:11:48 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] zed: the About window names Zeo's stage, the packaged commit
 and both repositories
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.18 (ask 38), on 0047. Before:

    Zeo 0.9.1
    Version: 0.9.1_p20261109
    Zed: 1.29.0+zeo

After, for a Zeo package:

    Zeo (αlpha)
    Version: 0.9.1_p20261109
    Zed: 1.29.0+f0d896f
    [Zeo] [Zed]   -- links to github.com/zeo-workspace/zeo and
                     github.com/zed-industries/zed

The title names the release stage instead of repeating the version,
which has its own row. The Zed row shows Zed's X.Y.Z with the packaged
upstream commit, shortened to 7 characters, from a new build-time
variable ZEO_UPSTREAM_COMMIT that the ebuild sets from EGIT_COMMIT.
ZED_COMMIT_SHA is deliberately not reused: it would also rewrite
AppVersion's build metadata, which extensions check compatibility
against, and feed AppCommitSha. Without the variable the row keeps
AppVersion as it is ("1.29.0+zeo"), and a development build without
RELEASE_VERSION keeps upstream's title and rows. Copy appends both
URLs. The window does not resize, so it grows by 32px for the links.

Test, seen failing first against stubs: zed::tests::
test_about_window_title_and_zed_row (the title for a package and for a
development build; the commit shortened; no commit and an empty
variable keep AppVersion).
---

